  "solution": {
    "text": "The surface area of the liquid drop is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>&#960;R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br />Its surface energy is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math><br /><br />When the drop splits in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>512</mn></math> droplets, the surface area of each droplet is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math> Total surface area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>A</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br />The volume of bigger drop is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> and volume of small droplets is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>512</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math><br /><br />Surface energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> is surface tension and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is area)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8901;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8901;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#8901;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>"
  }
